File Index

/normalizePluginModule.ts
Purpose: Normalizes plugin module structure and validates data types for consistent plugin handling.

/pluginCss.ts
Purpose: Manages dynamic CSS styling for plugins with unique identifiers.

/pluginHost.ts
Purpose: Manages plugin lifecycle, execution, and communication within the game client. Registration and syncInstalled are instance-preserving: a running plugin is never re-created just because the installed list changed. api.log/api.error stamp exactly one `[plugin:<id>]` prefix on each terminal line — plugins must not repeat their own id in the message.

/pluginHost.test.ts
Purpose: Pins that a running plugin instance survives installed-list churn and re-registration — plugin modules are closures, so a silent rebuild loses in-flight state (this is what broke text-to-speech).

/pluginConfigPersist.ts
Purpose: One-way event a running plugin uses to persist a config change it made ITSELF (a floating toggle button, not the config modal) — api.updateConfig is in-memory only and syncInstalled re-applies the saved userConfig over it, so an unpersisted self-toggle silently reverts. Sends a PATCH, never the whole runtime config (that would promote every default into an explicit saved value); MainContainer merges it onto the install record.

/pluginScriptRunner.ts
Purpose: Runs bundled plugin scripts as triggers, timers, or aliases within a runtime environment.

/registry.ts
Purpose: Registers and provides access to all core plugins for the game client.

/routed-gmcp-events.ts
Purpose: Defines all GMCP and custom game events routed through the client application.
